🇺🇸🇪🇺🇺🇦 US-European Missile Program, Stamped "Made in Ukraine"

▪️At face value it should be obvious Ukraine isn't and never will be making dozens of ballistic or air defense missiles/month in a war zone and when facilities come under regular Russian strikes;

▪️ These "Ukrainian" missiles are actually the product of a distributed US-European program built almost entirely outside of Ukraine;

▪️But with the "Ukraine" label via cutouts like "Firepoint," it creates plausible deniability when these US-European missiles are used on increasingly sensative targets deeper inside Russia;

▪️This allows the US to escalate while denying Russia the ability to strike directly back at either the US or its European proxies for now;

▪️As early as 2022 Western policymakers openly talked about this model of building "Ukrainian" missiles across Europe and transferring them quietly to Ukraine;

(image: "Firepoint's" FP-7 and FP-9 missiles)
